From 72764321beb361e36cdfd2a46020b9b89f965e48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SuperDistance <43229543+SuperDistance@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:16:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 61/62] serve: a long read gives way to a short request at the
 next chunk, not a chunk later or never (#656)

The server sends BYIELD for a waiting request under half as long only when a PP line (or the 10 s heartbeat) arrives,
and the engine looks for it at its next boundary. Where a boundary's own PP line is the only line for a while - every
chunk of a --batch read on one GPU, and #2050's pipelined pieces - the BYIELD answers that line and reaches the engine
after it has looked: the read gives way one boundary later, or never when that was the last one it could take. It is in
time only where the engine saves a periodic checkpoint after the PP line (every 16,384 tokens by default).

_control() now also calls on_quiet() whenever the engine has been quiet for half a second (its existing poll), and the
solo and admission reads run the same check there as at a PP line. A BYIELD for a read that has ended is ignored by
the engine, as before. serve/test_parallel.py: the fake engine takes --pp-every K (a PP line and a boundary every K
chunks); a solo read and an admission must give way at their first boundary (both fail on main), and the rule (only
to a much shorter request) holds on the poll too.

Measured on one RTX 5090 (Swift 1.5 IQ3_S, --batch 4, the engine built from main), main's server and this one, two
engine starts each (M F F M): a one-line request sent 0.2-8.6 s into a cold ~33K read, with nothing else decoding and
with one stream decoding. Late (a boundary passed after the request waited): 28 of 40 runs on main, 12 of which never
gave way; 4 of 40 with this change, all requests that started waiting 0.02-0.10 s before that boundary's PP line.
Where main was late the short request's TTFT went 3.56 -> 1.70 s (nothing decoding) and 4.40 -> 1.57 s (one stream);
where main never gave way 4.60 -> 1.51 s and 7.59 -> 2.35 s. Where both gave way at the same boundary, both requests'
TTFTs were the same (medians within 0.02 s). On 2x RTX 5090 with #2050's STRATA_PIPED_READ_PIECE=8192: 6 of 12 late without
it, none with it.

(cherry picked from commit ac21812c1a620b868102642e681aed99b2efd960)
